# SECURITY (codex finding #1): Never copy environment files into the
# Docker build context. They typically hold provider API keys, gateway
# auth tokens, and Postgres passwords; the build context becomes a layer
# inside the image, so a leaked or pulled image would expose them.
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
# Keys / certs that would similarly leak via image layers.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
# Lock files explicitly OK to copy — kept here as a hint that the deny
# list above is not exhaustive; if you add a new secret-bearing file
# pattern, list it here too.

# Keep high-volume prune guards after every re-inclusion rule. BuildKit can
# then stop walking these trees instead of reconsidering them for a later `!`.
.git
.claude
.assistant
.worktrees
node_modules
**/node_modules
target
**/target
artifacts
data
workspace
reports
**/coverage
**/coverage-*
**/dist
**/dist-node
**/bin
**/obj
